<article class="env-proposition" id="0716">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0716">Proposition <span data-tag="0716">9.7.5.3</span>.</a> In the situation of Construction <a data-tag="0715" href="/tag/0715">9.7.5.2</a>, suppose that the functors $F$ and $G$ exhibit $\widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ and $\widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}$ as $\widehat{\mathbb {K}}$-cocompletions of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ relative to $\mathbb {K}$, respectively (see Definition <a data-tag="06ZX" href="/tag/06ZX">9.7.1.16</a>). Then the functor $F \otimes G$ exhibits $\widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \otimes _{ \widehat{\mathbb {K}}} \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}$ as a $\widehat{\mathbb {K}}$-cocompletion of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ relative to $\mathbb {K}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}}$ be a $\widehat{\mathbb {K}}$-cocomplete $\infty $-category; we wish to show that precomposition with $F \otimes G$ induces an equivalence of $\infty $-categories 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Fun}^{  \widehat{\mathbb {K}} -\mathrm{cocont} }( \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \otimes _{ \widehat{\mathbb {K} } } \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}, \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}^{  \mathbb {K} -\mathrm{cocont} }( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}, \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} ). \]
</div>
<p>
       Invoking the universal property of the cocomplete tensor product (and the construction of $F \otimes G$), we can identify this with the functor 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Fun}^{  \widehat{\mathbb {K}}-\mathrm{Bil}}( \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \times \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}, \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}^{  \mathbb {K} -\mathrm{Bil}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\times \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}, \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} ) \]
</div>
<p>
       given by precomposition with $F \times G$. Using Remark <a data-tag="070A" href="/tag/070A">9.7.3.3</a>, we can rewrite this functor as a composition 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \begin{eqnarray*}  \operatorname{Fun}^{  \widehat{\mathbb {K} } -\mathrm{cocont} }( \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}, \operatorname{Fun}^{  \widehat{\mathbb {K} } -\mathrm{cocont}}( \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}, \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} ) ) &amp;  \xrightarrow { \circ F} &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}^{  \mathbb {K} -\mathrm{cocont} }( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{Fun}^{  \widehat{\mathbb {K} } -\mathrm{cocont} }( \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}, \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} ) ) \\ &amp;  \xrightarrow { \circ G} &amp;  \operatorname{Fun}^{  \mathbb {K} -\mathrm{cocont} }( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{Fun}^{  \mathbb {K} -\mathrm{cocont} }( \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}, \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} ) ) \end{eqnarray*}
</div>
<p>
       which is an equivalence by virtue of our assumptions on $F$ and $G$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
